      "writtenOn": "2022-07-26T08:49:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Andrew,\nIs the open-drain output pin in question among one of these two pins:\n1. GPIOA4 (EC_SOC_VCCST_PWRGD_OD)\n2. GPIOF1 (EC_PROCHOT_ODL)\nIf it is, the root cause of the incorrect level reading is that they are pulled up to an un-supported power rail (1.05 Voltage).\nPlease also refer to the comment #42 and #47 in the bug b:228222441 for the detailed.\nIn normal case, the level should be read correctly via PxDIN register no matter GPIO input or output.",
      "parentUuid": "4b0d3b2a_34f94ec2",
      "revId": "51e2296bca7c4ed9bbd1b34e39c2d4fdc5bb3a2b",
